 "heat": {
  "lines": [
   {
    "i": 29,
    "t0": 0.5,
    "t1": 8.021,
    "path": "out/narration/line_29.wav",
    "text": "Now let's make the release point perfect, exact to the last atom, and change just one thing: the temperature of the board.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      0.5,
      4.401
     ],
     [
      4.701,
      6.061
     ],
     [
      6.461,
      8.021
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 30,
    "t0": 8.721,
    "t1": 11.791,
    "path": "out/narration/line_30.wav",
    "text": "Where would the heat come from? The chips themselves.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      8.721,
      10.141
     ],
     [
      10.541,
      11.791
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 31,
    "t0": 12.27,
    "t1": 26.274,
    "path": "out/narration/line_31.wav",
    "text": "At the top, a chip holds about five joules of energy, just from its height. As it falls, that becomes speed. And every time it hits a pin, some of that speed turns into heat: in the pin, the board, and the chip.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      12.27,
      16.914
     ],
     [
      17.214,
      19.614
     ],
     [
      19.914,
      23.714
     ],
     [
      23.914,
      26.274
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 32,
    "t0": 26.874,
    "t1": 29.916,
    "path": "out/narration/line_32.wav",
    "text": "When it stops, all five joules have become heat.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      26.874,
      27.676
     ],
     [
      27.876,
      29.916
     ]
    ]
   },
   {
    "i": 33,
    "t0": 30.716,
    "t1": 44.128,
    "path": "out/narration/line_33.wav",
    "text": "Spread through the board, that warms it by less than a ten-thousandth of a degree. But warm wood and steel expand. The board grows by about a nanometre, the width of ten atoms, and every pin shifts with it.",
    "phrases": [
     [
      30.716,
      35.081
     ],
     [
      35.481,
      37.681
     ],
     [
      37.981,
      40.131
     ],
     [
